{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-har-pir-panela-l-semekanisme-i-sk-ytane-og-hj-rna-slik-som-pur-panela","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-har-pir-panela-l-semekanisme-i-sk-ytane-og-hj-rna-slik-som-pur-panela","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-har-pir-panela-l-semekanisme-i-sk-ytane-og-hj-rna-slik-som-pur-panela","_weak":true},"question":"Do PIR panels have locking mechanisms in joints and corners, like PUR panels?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-har-pir-panela-l-semekanisme-i-sk-ytane-og-hj-rna-slik-som-pur-panela-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-har-pir-panela-l-semekanisme-i-sk-ytane-og-hj-rna-slik-som-pur-panela-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Fresvik PIR and PUR panels have the same design and the same locking mechanism in joints and corners.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":4}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-i-kva-prosjekt-b-r-pir-f-retrekkjast-framfor-pur","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-i-kva-prosjekt-b-r-pir-f-retrekkjast-framfor-pur","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-i-kva-prosjekt-b-r-pir-f-retrekkjast-framfor-pur","_weak":true},"question":"In which projects should PIR be preferred over PUR?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-i-kva-prosjekt-b-r-pir-f-retrekkjast-framfor-pur-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-i-kva-prosjekt-b-r-pir-f-retrekkjast-framfor-pur-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"PIR should be preferred in projects where fire safety and risk reduction are especially important. This applies particularly to large cold and freezer stores, buildings with strict fire requirements, industrial and commercial buildings, projects where insurance companies have additional requirements, and facilities with high-value stored goods. If you are unsure which material is best, PIR is a safe choice because it provides extra fire safety while maintaining strong insulation performance.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":2}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kan-de-produsere-d-rer-og-portar-med-pir-skum","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kan-de-produsere-d-rer-og-portar-med-pir-skum","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kan-de-produsere-d-rer-og-portar-med-pir-skum","_weak":true},"question":"Can you produce doors and gates with PIR foam?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-de-produsere-d-rer-og-portar-med-pir-skum-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-de-produsere-d-rer-og-portar-med-pir-skum-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Yes. Fresvik supplies both doors and gates with PIR foam, using the same design as the PUR products.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":10}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kan-fresvik-produkt-levere-kj-le-og-fryserom-p-spesialm-l-eller-for-skreddarsydde-prosjekt","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kan-fresvik-produkt-levere-kj-le-og-fryserom-p-spesialm-l-eller-for-skreddarsydde-prosjekt","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kan-fresvik-produkt-levere-kj-le-og-fryserom-p-spesialm-l-eller-for-skreddarsydde-prosjekt","_weak":true},"question":"Can Fresvik Produkt deliver cold and freezer rooms to custom dimensions or tailor-made projects?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-fresvik-produkt-levere-kj-le-og-fryserom-p-spesialm-l-eller-for-skreddarsydde-prosjekt-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-fresvik-produkt-levere-kj-le-og-fryserom-p-spesialm-l-eller-for-skreddarsydde-prosjekt-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Yes. Fresvik Produkt delivers cold and freezer rooms adapted to each project. Panels and solutions can be produced to special dimensions so the room fits existing buildings, production premises or specific customer requirements. Solutions are adapted to special dimensions, technical requirements and larger or more complex facilities.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":12}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kan-pir-panel-brukast-ved-same-temperaturar-som-pur-panel","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kan-pir-panel-brukast-ved-same-temperaturar-som-pur-panel","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kan-pir-panel-brukast-ved-same-temperaturar-som-pur-panel","_weak":true},"question":"Can PIR panels be used at the same temperatures as PUR panels?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-pir-panel-brukast-ved-same-temperaturar-som-pur-panel-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-pir-panel-brukast-ved-same-temperaturar-som-pur-panel-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"PIR has a temperature range from -40 °C to +70 °C, while PUR tolerates -40 °C to +120 °C.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":8}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kan-pir-panela-produserast-i-same-storleik-som-pur-panela","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kan-pir-panela-produserast-i-same-storleik-som-pur-panela","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kan-pir-panela-produserast-i-same-storleik-som-pur-panela","_weak":true},"question":"Can PIR panels be produced in the same sizes as PUR panels?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-pir-panela-produserast-i-same-storleik-som-pur-panela-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kan-pir-panela-produserast-i-same-storleik-som-pur-panela-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Yes. Fresvik offers flexible room heights in 50 mm steps up to 8000 mm, with panel thicknesses of 75, 100, 125, 150 and 175 mm.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":9}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-korleis-er-vekta-densiteten-p-pir-panel-samanlikna-med-pur-panel","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-korleis-er-vekta-densiteten-p-pir-panel-samanlikna-med-pur-panel","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-korleis-er-vekta-densiteten-p-pir-panel-samanlikna-med-pur-panel","_weak":true},"question":"How does the weight/density of PIR panels compare with PUR panels?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-korleis-er-vekta-densiteten-p-pir-panel-samanlikna-med-pur-panel-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-korleis-er-vekta-densiteten-p-pir-panel-samanlikna-med-pur-panel-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"PUR panels have a density of 40 +/-2 kg/m3 and weigh approximately 13-17 kg/m2. PIR panels have a density of 42 +/-2 kg/m3 and weigh approximately 14-18.5 kg/m2.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":7}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kva-er-forskjellen-p-ein-kj-leromsd-r-og-ein-fryseromsd-r","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kva-er-forskjellen-p-ein-kj-leromsd-r-og-ein-fryseromsd-r","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kva-er-forskjellen-p-ein-kj-leromsd-r-og-ein-fryseromsd-r","_weak":true},"question":"What is the difference between a cold room door and a freezer room door?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-forskjellen-p-ein-kj-leromsd-r-og-ein-fryseromsd-r-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-forskjellen-p-ein-kj-leromsd-r-og-ein-fryseromsd-r-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"For standard cold and freezer room doors, the main difference is that the freezer room door has a heating cable in the frame. For industrial doors, the difference is in insulation and construction: a cold room door is designed for moderate temperatures, while a freezer room door is built for low freezing temperatures with thicker insulation, double gaskets and a heating cable in the frame to prevent gaskets from freezing.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":6}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kva-er-hovudforskjellen-mellom-pir-og-pur-i-kj-le-og-fryserom","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kva-er-hovudforskjellen-mellom-pir-og-pur-i-kj-le-og-fryserom","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kva-er-hovudforskjellen-mellom-pir-og-pur-i-kj-le-og-fryserom","_weak":true},"question":"What is the main difference between PIR and PUR in cold and freezer rooms?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-hovudforskjellen-mellom-pir-og-pur-i-kj-le-og-fryserom-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-hovudforskjellen-mellom-pir-og-pur-i-kj-le-og-fryserom-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"The main difference is in the fire properties. PIR generally has better fire resistance and lower smoke development than PUR, while both materials have very good insulation properties.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":1}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kva-er-kj-leromspanel-og-kva-tjukkleik-b-r-ein-velje-til-kj-l-og-fryserom","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kva-er-kj-leromspanel-og-kva-tjukkleik-b-r-ein-velje-til-kj-l-og-fryserom","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kva-er-kj-leromspanel-og-kva-tjukkleik-b-r-ein-velje-til-kj-l-og-fryserom","_weak":true},"question":"What are cold room panels, and which thickness should be chosen for cold and freezer rooms?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-kj-leromspanel-og-kva-tjukkleik-b-r-ein-velje-til-kj-l-og-fryserom-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-kj-leromspanel-og-kva-tjukkleik-b-r-ein-velje-til-kj-l-og-fryserom-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Cold room panels are insulated sandwich panels used for walls, ceilings and sometimes floors in cold and freezer rooms. The right thickness depends on room temperature and energy requirements. Cold rooms from 2 °C to 6 °C usually use 75-100 mm. Freezer rooms from 0 °C to -40 °C usually use 100-175 mm, depending on U-value and energy-efficiency requirements.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":11}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kva-er-pvc-gardin-og-n-r-b-r-ein-bruke-pvc-gardiner-i-kj-lerom-eller-fryserom","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kva-er-pvc-gardin-og-n-r-b-r-ein-bruke-pvc-gardiner-i-kj-lerom-eller-fryserom","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kva-er-pvc-gardin-og-n-r-b-r-ein-bruke-pvc-gardiner-i-kj-lerom-eller-fryserom","_weak":true},"question":"What is a PVC curtain, and when should PVC curtains be used in cold rooms or freezer rooms?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-pvc-gardin-og-n-r-b-r-ein-bruke-pvc-gardiner-i-kj-lerom-eller-fryserom-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kva-er-pvc-gardin-og-n-r-b-r-ein-bruke-pvc-gardiner-i-kj-lerom-eller-fryserom-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"PVC curtains are flexible PVC strips mounted in door openings to reduce heat loss and draught when the door is opened. They are often used in cold rooms and freezer rooms with frequent traffic. PVC curtains help reduce energy loss, maintain stable temperature, limit warm-air leakage and improve working comfort. For freezer rooms, low-temperature PVC is used. Fresvik supplies both fixed and sliding PVC curtains.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":5}
{"_id":"drafts.en-faqItem-faq-kvifor-har-pir-panel-nesten-same-u-verdi-som-pur-panel-men-betre-branneigenskapar","_type":"faqItem","language":"en","sourceLanguage":"nn","translationGroup":"fresvik:faqItem:faq-kvifor-har-pir-panel-nesten-same-u-verdi-som-pur-panel-men-betre-branneigenskapar","translatedFrom":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"faq-kvifor-har-pir-panel-nesten-same-u-verdi-som-pur-panel-men-betre-branneigenskapar","_weak":true},"question":"Why does a PIR panel have almost the same U-value as a PUR panel, but better fire properties?","answer":[{"_key":"en-faq-kvifor-har-pir-panel-nesten-same-u-verdi-som-pur-panel-men-betre-branneigenskapar-answer-0","_type":"block","style":"normal","children":[{"_key":"en-faq-kvifor-har-pir-panel-nesten-same-u-verdi-som-pur-panel-men-betre-branneigenskapar-answer-0-span","_type":"span","text":"Although PIR and PUR panels have almost the same U-value, PIR has better fire properties because the foam reacts by protecting the surface during fire and has higher thermal stability. PIR insulates well, but tolerates heat and fire significantly better than PUR. This is why PIR achieves fire class B, while PUR has class C.","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}],"category":"Customer service","order":3}
